# Content CMS And SEO

- Use concise, confident corporate language with concrete subjects and verifiable evidence.
- Avoid generic slogans and unsupported words such as leading, pioneering, world-class, or sustainable.
- Every published statistic must include value, unit, period, and source.
- Model relations between sectors, subsidiaries, projects, news, leadership, careers, partners, timeline, and sustainability.
- Keep slugs stable and unique; use references rather than duplicated content.
- Provide per-page title, description, canonical, Open Graph image, and indexability controls.
- Generate Organization, WebSite, BreadcrumbList, Article, and JobPosting schema where valid.
- Use meaningful image filenames and alt text based on purpose; decorative images use empty alt text.
- Draft, preview, internal API, and noncanonical filter URLs must not enter the public sitemap.
- Keep `[PLACEHOLDER]` visible in nonproduction content and block production release while required placeholders remain.
- Demo facts, legal copy, contact channels, domains, and policy text must be marked `DEMO_ONLY` or `LEGAL_VERIFY_*` until the owner supplies an approved source.
- Never convert a plausible-looking demo value into an official enterprise code, registered address, ownership statement, certification, financial claim, or legal conclusion.
- Production release is blocked while `[PLACEHOLDER]`, `DEMO_ONLY`, `LEGAL_VERIFY_*`, sample domains, or sample contacts remain in production-required content.
